Pipe Vice – 3D Assembly and Engineering Design

This project focuses on the design and development of a Pipe Vice assembly using SolidWorks. 
It involves creating individual mechanical components and integrating them into a complete assembly to represent the clamping mechanism used for securely holding pipes during machining and other workshop operations.

The design includes the Vice Base, Movable Jaw, Handle Bar, Handle Bar Caps, Screw Rod, and Set Screw. 
Each component was modeled with attention to dimensional accuracy, geometric features, and proper assembly relationships.
The project also incorporates detailed 2D engineering drawings for the complete assembly and individual components, including orthographic projections, sectional representations, and dimensioned views.


Project Specifications
CAD Software: SolidWorks
Design Category: Mechanical Component and Assembly Design
Main Assembly: Pipe Vice
Skills Applied: 3D Modeling, Component Design, Assembly Mates, Technical Drafting, and Engineering Visualization
